[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the graph
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - The graph has 3 edges: A→B, A→C, D→A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - This means:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m   - A is the parent of B and C.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m   - D is the parent of A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - So, the reachability is:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m   - A is upstream of B, C, and D (through A→B, A→C, D→A).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m   - B and C are descendants of A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m   - D is a descendant of A (through D→A).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m   - D is also a direct parent of A (through D→A), so A is a descendant of D (through D→A).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m   - B and C are descendants of A.
