[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - B: Is B a downstream of A? No. A is upstream of B, and the graph has edges B->A (i.e., B is upstream of A). Therefore, B is not a descendant of A. So B is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - C: Is C a descendant of A? No. A has no edges to C. So C is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - D: Is D a descendant of A? No. A has edges to B, but not to D. So D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m **Result:** A:0, B:0, C:0, D:0 → consistent with the observation.
