[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - B is perturbed, so B is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A is a descendant of B (B → A), so A is 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - C is not a descendant of B (B → A, B → C is not defined), so C is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - D is not a descendant of B, so D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m **Result**: A:1, B:0, C:0, D:0 → matches the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m ### 3. Perturb(C) -> A:1 B:1 C:0 D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - C is perturbed, so C is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - B is a descendant of C (C → B), so B is 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A is a descendant of B (B → A), so A is 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - D is not a descendant of C or B, so D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m **Result**: A:1, B:1, C:0, D:0 → matches the observation.
