[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m This seems to suggest that D is a descendant of B. But in the candidate graph, D is a descendant of B (from D->B), and B is a descendant of D (from B->D). But in the graph, the edge is B->A, B->C, D->B, D->C. That is, B is a parent of A and C, and D is a parent of B and C. So D is not a parent of B; rather, B is a parent of D. So D is a descendant of B, and B is a descendant of D. So the graph is: D -> B -> A and C, and B -> C.
