[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the semantics of the graph
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A node is **1** if it is a **downstream descendant** of the perturbed node.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A node is **0** if it is **not** a downstream descendant (i.e., it is an upstream node or an ancestor, or not connected).
