[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - Perturbed node: A
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A is the perturbed node, so A:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A is the source of the graph, so any node that is a descendant of A (B, C) will be 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - B is a descendant of A (A->B), so B:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - C is a descendant of B (B->C), so C:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - D is not a descendant of A (no edge from A to D), so D:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - Resulting values: A:0, B:1, C:1, D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - This matches the observed result: Perturb(A) -> A:0 B:1 C:1 D:0 ✅
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
