[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - Perturbed node: B
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - B is the perturbed node, so B:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - B is the source of the graph, so any node that is a descendant of B (C) will be 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - C is a descendant of B (B->C), so C:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A is not a descendant of B (no edge from B to A), so A:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - D is not a descendant of B (no edge from B to D), so D:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - Resulting values: A:0, B:0, C:1, D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - This matches the observed result: Perturb(B) -> A:0 B:0 C:1 D:0 ✅
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m #### Perturb(D)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - Perturbed node: D
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - D is the perturbed node, so D:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - D is the source of the graph, so any node that is a descendant of D (C) will be 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - C is a descendant of D (D->C), so C:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - A is not a descendant of D (no edge from D to A), so A:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=462400)[0m - B is not a descendant of D (no edge from D to B), so B:0.
